  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "In the numeration system with base \\(5,\\) counting is as follows: \\(1,\\) \\(2,\\) \\(3,\\) \\(4,\\) \\(10,\\) \\(11,\\) \\(12,\\) \\(13,\\) \\(14,\\) \\(20,\\) \\(\\ldots\\) The number whose description in the decimal system is \\(69,\\) when described in the base \\(5\\) system, is a number with:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "two consecutive digits"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "two non-consecutive digits"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "three consecutive digits"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "three non-consecutive digits"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "four digits"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1960-p16.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\[ 69=2\\cdot25+3\\cdot5+4, \\] its base-\\(5\\) representation is \\(234_5.\\) Its three digits \\(2,\\) \\(3,\\) and \\(4\\) are consecutive.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Express \\(69\\) using powers of \\(5\\)",
        "After finding the base-\\(5\\) digits, compare their values"
      ],
